# CODEOWNERS for the company brain.
# Each line: path pattern, then the GitHub handles that must review changes there.
# Replace the placeholders. The owner of a living document is also written in its
# frontmatter (`owner:`); keep the two in sync, this file is what GitHub enforces.

# Contracts and structure: a change here is a decision.
/AGENTS.md                 @{{owner-brain}}
/CLAUDE.md                 @{{owner-brain}}
/CODEOWNERS                @{{owner-brain}}
/_system/                  @{{owner-brain}}

# Living documents of the company.
/Knowledge/Company/        @{{owner-company}}
/Resources/Policies/       @{{owner-company}}
/Resources/Playbooks/      @{{owner-ops}}

# Decisions: the people who can accept one on the record.
/Decisions/                @{{owner-company}} @{{owner-brain}}

# Domain knowledge, one owner per domain.
/Knowledge/Product/        @{{owner-product}}
/Knowledge/Customers/      @{{owner-product}}
/Knowledge/Market/         @{{owner-company}}
/Knowledge/Engineering/    @{{owner-engineering}}
/Knowledge/Operations/     @{{owner-ops}}

# Relationships.
/CRM/                      @{{owner-company}}

# Everything else (inputs, projects, journal, output) needs no mandatory review.
